In public/js/pose-stage.js (the PoseStage class) add a hand zoom and keep the figure in frame (STU-PE1). SEARCH/REPLACE edits only, change nothing else:
1. In the constructor state add `this.zoom = 'body';`.
2. Replace the body of refit() with:
      const w = K.fk.solve(this.pose);
      const view = K.project.makeView({ yaw: this.yaw, pitch: this.pitch, width: this.canvas.width, height: this.canvas.height }, w);
      if (this.zoom === 'body') {
        this.frame = { scale: view.scale, center: view.center };
      } else {
        // a hand fills the canvas: 5 times the body scale, centred on its middle knuckle
        this.frame = { scale: view.scale * 5, center: w.pos[`${this.zoom}_middle_mcp`] };
      }
      this.lastView = this.lastViewPixels = view;
3. Add a method after setShow(mode):
    setZoom(zoom) {
      // 'body', 'l' or 'r'
      this.zoom = zoom;
      this.refit();
      this.draw(false);
    }
4. Add a method `outOfFrame()` that returns true when, with w = K.fk.solve(this.pose) and the full-size view `K.project.makeView({ yaw: this.yaw, pitch: this.pitch, width: this.canvas.width, height: this.canvas.height, scale: this.frame.scale, center: this.frame.center }, w)`, any point of w.pos has toScreen x < 0, y < 0, x > width or y > height. In the body zoom only (when this.zoom !== 'body' return false).
5. In apply(), right before `this.draw(!commit);` insert: `if (commit && this.frame && this.outOfFrame()) this.refit();`. In the pointerup and pointercancel handlers, right before `self.draw(false);` insert: `if (self.outOfFrame()) self.refit();`.
